{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show 9f9eeef:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/round3.retained-rows.report.md | nl -ba'","aggregated_output":"     1\t<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (high), agent a5e106319fe97c022; saved by the coordinator -->\n     2\t\n     3\t## `retainedRows(frame)` on every store: done\n     4\t\n     5\t`AlignedStore`, `PointStore` and `DonutStore` now have `retainedRows(frame: Frame): ArrayLike<number> | null`. The two waiting controller tests pass with no change to them or to the controller. Nothing is committed and no build was run.\n     6\t\n     7\t### What the method returns\n     8\t- The source row indexes that this revision's `source.rowAt` still answers, ascending. That is two parts:\n     9\t  - the rows still retained below the frame's end;\n    10\t  - the evicted rows kept for that revision (archived with a last-seen revision at or after it).\n    11\t- `null` when the revision is retired, or when it isn't one this store published (an uncommitted preview, another store's frame).\n    12\t- Imputed-zero rows and rows with an unplaceable x are source rows, so they are listed.\n    13\t\n    14\t### Cost\n    15\t- Proportional to the rows currently retained plus the evicted rows still kept for live revisions. There is no scan over evicted history.\n    16\t- When nothing is archived for the revision, the result is a view over the retained index, not a copy. Otherwise one sorted merge into a new array.\n    17\t\n    18\t### Where\n    19\t- `src/data/store-rows.ts`:\n    20\t  - `RowRevisions.retainedRows` finds the window that published the frame's revision;\n    21\t  - `RowWindow.retainedRows` does the work;\n    22\t  - `StreamRows.retainedIndexes` and `FrameSource.limit` are small new accessors.\n    23\t- `src/data/store.ts`, `src/data/store-unaligned.ts`: the public method on each store.\n    24\t\n    25\t### Tests\n    26\tIn `test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts`. They were written first and failed because the method did not exist.\n    27\t- **Property, for line, scatter and donut (400 runs each).** Inputs:\n    28\t  - an opening as object rows or typed columns;\n    29\t  - up to 8 appends with `keep`;\n    30\t  - late arrivals from negative x steps;\n    31\t  - null, absent and numeric y under both `missing` policies;\n    32\t  - rows whose x can't be placed.\n    33\t\n    34\t  For the current frame and every older frame still held, the list is strictly ascending and equals exactly the indexes `rowAt` answers. A frame retired along the way gives `null`.\n    35\t- **A preview and another store's frame** give `null`. After commit the same store lists `[0, 1, 2]`.\n    36\t\n    37\t### Controller tests (`test/core/round3.test.ts`, unchanged)\n    38\t- ✓ \"a retained imputed-zero row behind an evicted source index is re-read while paused\"\n    39\t- ✓ \"R7: x 10000 kept with the newest of 1,000 late arrivals (keep 2): re-encoding reads the two rows, not 1,002 indexes\"\n    40\t\n    41\t### Runs\n    42\t- `npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/data packages/axylo/test/core`:\n    43\t  ```\n    44\t  Tests  428 passed (428)\n    45\t  Duration  7.63s\n    46\t  ```\n    47\t- `npm run typecheck`: no errors. The probe file error you mentioned did not appear.\n    48\t- Whole Node suite: `Tests  1 failed | 1507 passed (1508)`. The one failure is the timing bound in `test/simplify/simplify.test.ts` (\"keeps a million-slot outlier…\", 32.5 ms against 30). It is a load-dependent flake I've seen before, not in my modules.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
