{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show 9f9eeef:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/round3.lookup.report.md | nl -ba'","aggregated_output":"     1\t<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (high), agent a5e106319fe97c022; saved by the coordinator -->\n     2\t\n     3\t## Round 3: lookup and data author\n     4\t\n     5\tAll three items are done. The new lookup methods compile and their tests pass; I sent `main` the one-line notice right after they compiled. Nothing is committed; no shared build was touched.\n     6\t\n     7\t### 1. `members`, `has`, `slot`, and `rule`: done\n     8\tThe methods couldn't be called before they existed, so these tests are new rather than failing first.\n     9\t\n    10\t**What each lookup does now:**\n    11\t- **Scatter**, exact and lattice:\n    12\t  - The pointer index now enumerates a group from its first ref: that point first, then the other points at the same position, then every other position within 0.5 px, in a fixed order that doesn't depend on where the pointer is.\n    13\t  - `pick` builds its `refs` from that same enumeration, so `members(target, 0, 8)` equals `target.refs` and the tooltip's rows.\n    14\t  - Paging skips whole positions and whole tree buckets by their counts. A page costs about `from + count` reads plus at most one 32-entry leaf.\n    15\t  - `has` is a single distance check between two grid entries.\n    16\t  - `rule` is set only on lattice picks (`rule: 'lattice'`). Absent means exact, per the contract, so existing tests comparing whole targets still pass.\n    17\t  - A ref rebuilt by the caller is found without walking points that share its x: directly when the series has no row index, or through a row map built with the lookup for any series with a run of more than 32 equal x values.\n    18\t  - Points clipped by the plot are not in the index, so they are never members.\n    19\t  - `slot` returns the point's index in its `PointSeries`, or −1.\n    20\t- **Aligned:** `members` returns the visible series at that x, in tooltip order (paged); `has` checks visible series and the same x; `slot` is the x slot, or −1.\n    21\t- **Donut:** `members` returns the slice itself; `slot` is the slice's index in `view.slices`. An \"Other\" slice stands for several frame categories; `view.slices[slot].members` lists them.\n    22\t\n    23\t**Tests** (`test/lookup/scatter.test.ts`):\n    24\t- **Property, 800 runs:** two interleaved series of near-coincident points with shuffled rows, at ratios 1, 2, exact, and with the lattice forced. Checks:\n    25\t  - `members` over the full count has each member once, starts with the first ref, and has `count` entries;\n    26\t  - pages of three concatenate to the whole list;\n    27\t  - `members(0, 8)` equals `refs` and the tooltip's rows;\n    28\t  - `has` agrees with `members` for every ref, rebuilt refs included;\n    29\t  - `slot` agrees with the frame.\n    30\t- **I8:** a point clipped by the y domain next to two drawn ones. The count is 2; `has` is false for the clipped point and `members` leaves it out.\n    31\t- **R3:** on the 32,000-point ring at ratio 1 the rule is lattice and the count is 14. `members(target, 8, 8)` gives the other six, none of them on page one, all with `has` true.\n    32\t- **R5:** on 50,000 coincident points with an explicit row index, `has` with rebuilt refs walks no points (the walk counter `work.locations` stays 0). `members(target, 8, 8)` reads at most 32 entries (new `lastMembersRead` counter).\n    33\t- Aligned and donut cases are in the same file.\n    34\t- Mutation check: a wrong `has` fails the property test.\n    35\t\n    36\t### 2. R13: fixed in `src/data`; the controller needs nothing new\n    37\t- The failing test, written first: a line over two 10-entry `Float64Array` columns, memory hook read before the first frame. It reported 170 B; the expected 10 B is the slot states.\n    38\t- `resolveTable` now records the buffers of every typed column a caller gives, in a weak set. `ByteCount` never counts those buffers, whatever frames or store are counted.\n    39\t- `CallerBuffers` keeps its API, so `instrument.ts` works unchanged. Its `add(table)` call is now redundant but harmless.\n    40\t\n    41\t### 3. I13: a helper for the jump field\n    42\t- The interaction author's uncommitted tree already adds `missingX` to their last-resort scan in `jumpTarget`. That scan still includes rows the table doesn't print: missing-y rows outside the view, whose x `pageForX` still maps to a page.\n    43\t- New `printedX(view, formatters, matches)` in `src/reader/table.ts`. It returns the smallest x among exactly the rows the table prints, formatted as the table formats them: points of every series in view, plus missing-y rows inside the x domain; slots in view on aligned charts.\n    44\t- The failing test, written first (the export didn't exist yet): a date scatter with missing-y rows inside and outside the view. Every printed x is found and its page holds it; an x outside the view is not found.\n    45\t- **For the interaction author** (no interface between us changes; it's a new export): replace `written()` with `printedX(view, d.formatters, w => normalized(w) === want)`.\n    46\t\n    47\t### Size\n    48\tRelease-settings esbuild bundle of `src/index.ts`, minified, gzip level 9:\n    49\t\n    50\t| Bundle | Minified | Gzipped |\n    51\t|---|---:|---:|\n    52\t| HEAD | 340,228 B | 119,959 B |\n    53\t| HEAD plus only my files | 343,199 B | 121,036 B |\n    54\t\n    55\tMy pass adds about 1,077 B gzipped. `printedX` is tree-shaken until something imports it. The interaction author removing `groupRefs` and similar code should offset part of this.\n    56\t\n    57\t### Runs\n    58\t- `npm run typecheck`: no errors.\n    59\t- `npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/lookup`: `Tests  71 passed (71)`.\n    60\t- data, lookup, scene, view, reader and layout together: `Tests  421 passed (421)`.\n    61\t- Whole Node suite: `Test Files  1 failed | 68 passed (69)`, `Tests  2 failed | 1499 passed (1501)`. Both failures are in `test/core/round3.test.ts`, the controller author's untracked file, still in progress; it had 6 failures earlier, and they also failed with my R13 change reverted. A later run of that file alone showed three:\n    62\t  - \"a retained imputed-zero row behind an evicted source index is re-read while paused\" (`[5, 7]` against `[5, 7, 10]`);\n    63\t  - \"R7: … re-encoding reads the two rows, not 1,002 indexes\" (1001 against at most 10);\n    64\t  - \"a 195 px scatter … zoom to −1000…1500\" (`[−500, 1500]` against `[−1000, 1500]`).\n    65\t\n    66\t  The first two may need something from the stores. If the controller's author needs a store change for them, tell me what.\n    67\t\n    68\t### Files\n    69\t- `packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts`, `scatter.ts`, `aligned.ts`, `donut.ts`\n    70\t- `packages/axylo/src/data/store-bytes.ts`, `options.ts`\n    71\t- `packages/axylo/src/reader/table.ts`\n    72\t- Tests: `packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts`, `packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts`, `packages/axylo/test/reader/index.test.ts`\n    73\t\n    74\tThe private size-build directory is removed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show 9f9eeef:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/round3.common.md | nl -ba'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Round 3: the narrow re-check's findings (common part, read first)\n     2\t\n     3\tThe cross-provider re-check of the blocking defects is `reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/blockers-recheck.review.md` (Codex gpt-6.2-sol, max, read-only, at e90d8db). It confirms most blockers closed, lists what is still partly fixed (table 1) and fourteen regressions from the last round (table 2, R1 to R14). Its blocking list: C2, I4, I5, R1, R2. Read the whole review, then your own section below.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe coordinator's own verification of e90d8db on the shared build: every core browser suite on SVG, 920 passed, 4 failed, 1 skipped (925); chart and a11y on canvas, 280 passed, 3 skipped. The four failures: three acceptance A2 toolbar tests that do not know the Select range button yet (the acceptance author updates them), and acceptance I1 donut \"the tooltip can itself be hovered\": after Escape from a hold, moving to the first datum and then to another one, the other one's tooltip does not open (the interaction author's, see the Escape clarification).\n     6\t\n     7\t## Coordinator's decisions for this round\n     8\t\n     9\t1. **The lookup is the only place that knows what a group is.** Five findings over three reviews (C8, I7, I8, R3, R5) come from code outside the lookup rebuilding a scatter group by another rule. The contract (`packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts`, already edited by me) now has `Lookup.members(target, from, count)`, `Lookup.has(target, ref)` and `Lookup.slot(ref)`, and the point target carries an optional `rule: 'exact' | 'lattice'`. The lookup's author implements them first; until that lands, `tsc` is red in `src/lookup` only. Then: paging, dismissal and row selection use `members` and `has` (the interaction author deletes `groupRefs` and its like), and the hover payload uses `slot` instead of searching the run or rereading the caller's row (the controller's author).\n    10\t2. **Decision 0004, clarification on Escape rewritten** (`docs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md`, \"Clarifications after the verification\"): after Escape from a hold, the held datum and the datum under the pointer are both dismissed; a dismissed datum stays closed until the pointer reaches a datum other than itself; Escape from a pin or a plain hover dismisses only the datum on show.\n    11\t3. **Compact bar patterns (C13) are accepted as they are.** Spec A5 now says neighbouring compact bar series differ by pattern and series further apart may share one. Nothing to do.\n    12\t4. **Mixed languages on the plot's proxy (part of I13)** are accepted as a limit: one element has one language; the reading's language wins. Nothing to do.\n    13\t5. Pointer tolerance (R9): the one-pixel rule of the decision is in viewport pixels. The interaction layer applies it before converting to layout pixels (a pointer within 1 viewport px outside the plot's viewport rectangle is moved onto its edge), for picking and for range ends alike. The lookup's own 1 layout-px slack stays.\n    14\t\n    15\t## Rules, as always\n    16\t\n    17\t`AGENTS.md`. Stay in your files. For every item, write the test that fails on the current code first (the reviewer's sequence; expected values from the spec or the decision), then fix. If a sequence does not fail as described, say what you saw and change nothing. Keep it small: the library is 19 KiB over its size target, so prefer removing a special case to adding one, and say what your pass does to the gzipped size (a release-settings build of HEAD against your tree is enough).\n    18\t\n    19\tShared build: `packages/axylo/dist` is built from the current commit and only the coordinator rebuilds it. Use a private directory inside the project with `AXYLO_BUNDLE` for browser tests and remove it afterwards. Do not commit. Never kill by pattern. The machine restarted once today: keep nothing you need in the system /tmp.\n    20\t\n    21\tReport: per item, the failing test written first and what changed, or what you observed instead; last lines of each run; size before and after; what is not done.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
