diately. A reordered focused slice can still blur. The date fallback skips `missingX` rows printed by the scatter table, and independently worded proxy labels still share the reading’s language. [interaction.ts:281](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:281), [interaction.ts:1605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1605), [interaction.ts:1836](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1836), [reader/table.ts:134](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/table.ts:134) | The all-zero slice, Arabic/German jump, and immediate `lang` tests use F8, A4, A10, fixtures and `Intl`. **None** for reordering, missing-y date jumps or mixed-language names. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:371](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:371) |\n    44\t| C14 · Scatter keeps a redundant x column after eviction | Minor | **Fixed** | The store drops `positions` when all retained positions are represented by point x values again. [store-unaligned.ts:195](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:195) | “Drops the scatter x positions column once every retained row is a point again.” Fixture for retained x and an implementation-specific buffer check consistent with P7. [streaming-storage.test.ts:817](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:817) |\n    45\t\n    46\t## Table 2. Regressions introduced since `bbd7564`\n    47\t\n    48\t| Severity | Sequence | Wrong result | Smallest fix |\n    49\t|---|---|---|---|\n    50\t| **R1 · Blocker** | Pin Q3 in Q1–Q4. Press its row, append Q5 with `keep: 4`, then release over the surviving Q3 button. | Release selects **Q4**. The handler uses Q3’s old numeric category index. Its one-second suppression also swallows unrelated keyboard clicks. [tooltip.ts:150](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:150), [tooltip.ts:216](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:216), [interaction.ts:1942](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1942) | Capture the semantic row identity, resolve its current ref on release, and suppress only the matching pointer click. |\n    51\t| **R2 · Blocker** | Create A first in a shadow root. Pin A, hover B without moving focus, then press Escape. | B spends Escape while focus is inside A. The ownership check sees A’s host. The drag branch can spend the key before checking ownership at all. [interaction.ts:1525](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1525) | Resolve the focused chart through the composed tree before any branch spends Escape. |\n    52\t| **R3 · Major** | At DPR 1, pin the centre pick of the 32,000-point ring and press `+6 more`. | The winning group has 14 rows. All six shown on page two belong to another lattice group. [focus.ts:174](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:174), [scatter-grid.ts:313](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:313) | Page directly from the winning grid group using the same exact or lattice coordinates as the pick. |\n    53\t| **R4 · Major** | Pin A, move over unrelated B, press Escape, then move within B. | B stays suppressed even though only A was pinned. The clarification that dismisses both datums applies to a corridor hold. [interaction.ts:1552](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1552) | Add the physical pick to the dismissal set only when dismissing a hold. |\n    54\t| **R5 · Major** | Dismiss scatter A, append 49,999 coincident B rows, then move within the group. | A is outside the sample, so each dismissal membership check walks the group. One check took **50,001 lookup steps**, and a move can check twice. [interaction.ts:1192](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1192), [interaction.ts:774](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:774) | Test the saved ref directly against the winning group’s membership predicate. |\n    55\t| **R6 · Major** | Draw scatter from a row getter that succeeds during normalization. Make it throw after drawing, then hover the point with a subscriber. | Hover throws and delivers no event. The payload rereads the raw getter even though the lookup already resolved the normalized point. [controller.ts:1716](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1716), [controller.ts:1982](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1982) | Reuse the lookup’s cached point index and normalized y. |\n    56\t| **R7 · Major** | Keep scatter x=10,000 and the newest late arrival with `keep: 2`. After 1,000 late arrivals, Pause, append, and change the y label. | Re-encoding reads **1,002 source indexes for two displayed rows**. The scan spans the evicted history between retained indexes. [controller.ts:842](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:842) | Enumerate the actual retained indexes of the displayed revision. This also fixes the sparse-window omission in C4. |\n    57\t| **R8 · Major** | At 195 px, draw scatter x=`−3.3, 7.7, 1001.5`. Use Select range at the drawn positions −1,000 and 1,500. | The drawn domain is `[−1000, 2000]`, but the toggle clamps to `[-500, 1500]`, treats the selection as the entire range, and does nothing. [layout/index.ts:279](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/index.ts:279), [interaction.ts:1386](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1386) | Use one effective x domain for projection, gesture bounds, and controller zoom clamping. |\n    58\t| **R9 · Major** | Scale the chart horizontally to `0.5`. Point at a fractional left-edge mark whose viewport x is 336.96 and arrives as 336. | The 0.96 viewport px rounding error becomes 1.92 layout px and the pick is rejected. Select range also rejects rounded releases just outside an edge. [interaction.ts:710](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:710), [lookup/geometry.ts:17](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/geometry.ts:17), [interaction.ts:1389](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1389) | Apply the decision’s one-pixel tolerance in viewport coordinates before conversion, and use the same edge clamp for range endpoints. |\n    59\t| **R10 · Major** | Narrow to Q3 in Q1–Q4. Give Q3 and Q4 the same formatted x and y text. Append Q5–Q7 with `keep: 4`. | Focus moves to Q4 but the spoken text stays at “Point 3 of 4” instead of “Point 1 of 4.” The two data readings compare equal. [focus.ts:215](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:215), [interaction.ts:1932](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1932) | Compare the raw category key and use exact remapping for the last spoken identity. |\n    60\t| **R11 · Major** | Start with 135 px of plot room and a 98 px strip. Resize to 134 px of room while responsive CSS reduces the strip to 48 px and leaves the axis style unchanged. | Readout stays `none`. A fresh chart with those dimensions reserves the strip and draws an 86 px plot. [controller.ts:1414](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1414) | Invalidate the strip measurement on resize or a change to its computed style. |\n    61\t| **R12 · Major** | Draw a wide scatter with x `1.1, 8.9, 10.7` and an x tick formatter that throws above 12. | Every drawn tick formats successfully, but AX160 is published because unused coarser candidates invoke the formatter above 12. [axes.ts:160](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:160), [controller.ts:1348](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1348) | Track formatter failures with their candidate sets and publish failures from the fitted layout. |\n    62\t| **R13 · Major** | Create a line from two 10-entry `Float64Array` columns and read the memory hook before the first frame. | The hook reports **170 B** owned, including **160 B** of borrowed columns. Only the 10 state bytes belong to the library. [instrument.ts:151](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/instrument.ts:151), [controller.ts:1908](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1908) | Register caller buffers from every counted frame, including pending frames. |\n    63\t| **R14 · Minor** | Set Select range’s first endpoint, start a drag, then let an append redraw before releasing. | The redraw replaces the drag rectangle with the old first-end marker. [interaction.ts:1294](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1294), [interaction.ts:2015](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:2015) | Skip the endpoint repaint while dragging. |\n    64\t\n    65\tFor C13, a fill-pattern fix requires extending `RectMark.pattern` beyond its current four values and rendering the added patterns in Canvas and SVG. [contracts.ts:469](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:469)\n    66\t\n    67\t**Release acceptance may not start.** The blocking list is **C2**, unbounded retention across paused hide/show cycles, **I4**, clipped pinned-strip rows or paging controls, **I5**, incomplete composed clipping and painted-outline protection, **R1**, a pressed row selecting the wrong category, and **R2**, Escape going to the wrong chart.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
