{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show 9f9eeef:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/round3.interaction.report.md | nl -ba'","aggregated_output":"     1\t<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (high), agent aa0e6fca8e4a6224b; saved by the coordinator -->\n     2\t\n     3\t## Round 3 (interaction): result\n     4\t\n     5\tEvery item has a change and a test, except where noted. I wrote each test against the committed code first; on a bundle of HEAD before my edits, 13 browser tests and 1 Node test fail and pass after the fix. Several tests also passed on the old code, so they prove less — listed in the table and under \"What this does not cover\". Nothing is committed, the shared `dist` was not touched, and every probe and scratch file is removed. The a11y probe that broke `npm run typecheck` for everyone has been deleted.\n     6\t\n     7\tTwo things are not mine or not done:\n     8\t- **R8, controller's half:** two clicks at −1,000 and 1,500 now request `[-1000, 1500]`. On the build I tested (before c29e566) the controller clamped that to `[-500, 1500]`, so the drawn domain stayed `[-2000, 2000]`. My test asserts only that the request is made; it needs your re-check on the shared build.\n     9\t- **R5 cost test:** dismissal now goes through `lookup.has`. I did not write a test that 49,999 appended points are not walked.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Per item\n    12\t\n    13\tNew browser tests are in `test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts` unless named otherwise.\n    14\t\n    15\t| Item | Test written first | Old code | What changed |\n    16\t|---|---|---|---|\n    17\t| 1 Groups from the lookup | \"nine exactly coincident points with clipped points interleaved: page two lists the ninth\" | **fails** | `groupRefs` deleted from `core/focus.ts`. Paging uses `lookup.members`, dismissal uses `lookup.has`. Rebuilt targets keep the pick's `rule`. Node tests in focus-reading now call `lookup.members`. |\n    18\t| 1 (ring) | \"32,000-point ring: page two in the winning device pixel\" | passes | Does not reproduce in the browser at this size; kept as a guard. |\n    19\t| 2 Escape | Donut replica of the acceptance sequence; \"R4: pin A, over B, Escape, move within B: B opens\" | **both fail** | A dismissed datum now lapses only when the pointer or keyboard reaches a datum other than itself. Escape from a hold closes the held datum and the one under the pointer. Escape from a pin closes only the pin, which stays shown until the pointer moves. |\n    20\t| 3 R1 | \"pin Q3, press its row, append Q5 with keep 4, release: Q3\"; \"pointer press on one row, then Enter on another: both selected\" | **both fail** | A press captures the row entry, and release selects that entry's current (remapped) row. Only the pointer's own click (`detail > 0`) is swallowed. |\n    21\t| 4 R2 | \"A in a shadow root, created first: pin A, hover B, Escape: A's pin closes, B stays\" | **fails** | New `activeElementOf` in `dom/attributes.ts` follows `shadowRoot.activeElement`; used for Escape ownership (decided before the drag branch), focus hand-off and teardown. With focus in no chart, a dragging chart owns Escape. |\n    22\t| 5 I4 | \"long category name in a narrow strip: title cut, row and pager inside, or nothing\"; \"a strip of which only a sliver is visible is not shown\" | **both fail** | The strip is shown only if its title, first row and pinned \"+N more\" lie wholly inside its box and its ancestors' clip. The viewport does not count, because a strip in the page flow can be scrolled to. The strip's title is one line with an ellipsis (`theme/css.ts`). |\n    23\t| 6 I5 | \"chart slotted into a component whose shadow wrapper clips: tooltip stays inside\" | **fails** | The clipping walk goes through `assignedSlot`. The control focus-outline allowance is 3 px times the mapping's scale; no test for that. |\n    24\t| 7 R8 | \"195 px scatter, unzoomed: a wheel zooms around the pointer within the drawn domain\" | **fails** (off by 1,000 units) | One helper, `zoomBounds`, now serves Select range, drag, pinch, wheel, keys and pan: `view.xFull` while zoomed, the projection's domain unzoomed. |\n    25\t| 7 R8 (two clicks) | \"Select range −1000 to 1500 asks for that zoom\" | passes | My half only; see above. |\n    26\t| 8 R9 | \"scaled to 0.5: whole viewport pixel left of the edge picks the edge mark\" | **fails** | Points within 1 viewport px outside the plot rectangle are moved onto its edge before converting to layout pixels, for picks and range ends. |\n    27\t| 9 R10 | Node test (focus-reading): Q3 and Q4 formatted alike read differently | **fails** | `datumReading` uses the raw category key, and the last spoken datum is remapped exactly. |\n    28\t| 10 R14 | \"first end set, drag, append before release: selection stays the drag's\" | **fails** | No first-end repaint during a drag. |\n    29\t| 11 I6 | \"after a switch into the strip and a 300 ms rest there, the corridor holds\" | passes | A presentation switch restarts the rest for the still pointer; a committed anchor change on the same pick restarts it too. A tooltip-rectangle change alone does not yet restart it. |\n    30\t| 12 I13 | \"reordered all-zero slices keep focus\" | **fails** | Focus is restored after reordering the slice list. |\n    31\t| 12 I13 (jump) | \"missing-y date can be jumped to\" | passes | The last-resort scan in \"Jump to\" now calls the reader's `printedX`. |\n    32\t| 13 | I2 narrowed secondary ref survives a redraw and Resume (Pause and Resume from the keyboard, since a click elsewhere ends a pin by rule 4); I3 pinch with no zoom ends the pin and hover works | both pass on old | Missing tests added. Still missing: a scaled control outline. |\n    33\t\n    34\t## Runs (private bundle, then removed)\n    35\t\n    36\t| Run | Result |\n    37\t|---|---|\n    38\t| `npm run typecheck` | clean |\n    39\t| `npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/core` | 16 files, 262 passed |\n    40\t| chart + a11y, SVG | 301 passed, 1 failed (302) |\n    41\t| chart + a11y, canvas | 297 passed, 1 failed, 4 skipped (302) |\n    42\t| `final-*`, Firefox | 94 passed, 3 failed, 2 skipped (99) |\n    43\t| `final-*`, WebKit | 94 passed, 3 failed, 2 skipped (99) |\n    44\t| round3 + partials after fixing those 3 | chromium 28 passed; Firefox 26 passed, 2 skipped; WebKit 26 passed, 2 skipped |\n    45\t\n    46\t- The single SVG and canvas failure is the known `ensureStyles` artefact under `AXYLO_BUNDLE`; the 4 canvas skips are SVG-only tests.\n    47\t- The 3 Firefox/WebKit failures were the R9 test using a fractional pointer (now whole pixels) and two CDP pinch tests. The pinch tests now carry `requireEngineFeature(['chromium'])`, so they are skipped there.\n    48\t- Acceptance was not run, since it needs the shared build.\n    49\t- `test/core/round3.test.ts` (the controller author's) had 2 failures mid-run; the final core run passed all 262.\n    50\t\n    51\t**Size**, release-settings rebuild of HEAD c29e566 against HEAD plus my files: everything 118,941 → 119,275 B (+334 B gzipped); line only 99,405 → 99,716 B (+311 B).\n    52\t\n    53\t## What this does not cover\n    54\t\n    55\t- Fully confirming R8 (controller's half).\n    56\t- Tests for R5's cost, a scaled control outline, and the I6 tooltip-rectangle case.\n    57\t- The ring, I6, the two-click R8 request and the missing-y jump tests pass on the old code too, so they guard against regressions but do not prove those fixes.\n    58\t\n    59\t## Files\n    60\t\n    61\t- **Source:** `src/dom/{interaction,tooltip,mapping,attributes,table,toolbar}.ts`, `src/core/focus.ts`, `src/theme/css.ts`.\n    62\t- **Tests:** `test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts` (new), `test/browser/chart/final-partials.browser.test.ts`, `test/core/focus-reading.test.ts`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
