browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:170) |\n    26\t| C4 · Paused re-encoding loses findings or raw rows | Major | **Partly fixed** | The reported AX130, null-x and typed-NaN cases are covered. The displayed window’s option findings are discarded, so strict accepts a field available only in held rows and blanks the plot. The backward scan also misses a retained imputed-zero row behind an evicted source index. [controller.ts:645](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:645), [controller.ts:842](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:842) | “A ninth series held,” “a displayed row with x null,” and “a NaN in a typed column.” §3.5, F2, I6 and fixtures. **None** for displayed-only AX101 or sparse source indexes. [verify-pass.test.ts:95](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:95) |\n    27\t| C5 · Frozen scatter loses month precision | Major | **Fixed** | Date precision reads through the owned-row accessor used for event payloads. [controller.ts:1126](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1126), [controller.ts:1952](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1952) | “March (YYYY-MM) queued with keep 1…” F4 and fixture. The assertion checks the year and absence of a day number. [verify-pass.test.ts:145](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:145) |\n    28\t| C6 · Throwing or re-entrant getter bypasses strict or teardown | Major | **Partly fixed** | The three reported row-getter paths are covered by per-call preparation and liveness checks. A throwing option getter still runs in `preview()` before strict is set. A strict chart then accepts AX199 and shows the error state. [controller.ts:565](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:565), [controller.ts:595](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:595), [controller.ts:717](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:717) | “Strict: an append whose x getter throws,” “a getter that runs a nested update,” and “a getter that destroys the chart.” DX5 and §3.5. **None** for a throwing option getter. [verify-pass.test.ts:164](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:164) |\n    29\t| C7 · Scatter does data-sized work on pointer move | Major | **Partly fixed** | The fallback lattice is built with the lookup for the reported ring. Payload construction still walks equal-y or unrecognized-y runs. A hover on the latest of 50,000 coincident points read **50,000 row indexes**. [scatter-grid.ts:348](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:348), [controller.ts:1982](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1982) | “The first pick at the centre of a 32,000-point ring” and “50,000 points at one x.” The work caps are test-selected. The latter fixture uses distinct numeric y values and takes its expected y from the normalized column. **None** for coincident payload cost. [scatter.test.ts:631](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:631), [verify-pass.test.ts:223](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:223) |\n    30\t| C8 · Lattice paging repeats page one | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | The reported ring now has a second page, but it contains six rows outside the winning lattice group. See R3. [focus.ts:174](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:174), [interaction.ts:739](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:739) | **None** for the ring’s second page. “Ten coincident points … +2 more” checks an exact group, and the lattice oracle checks only the initial pick. [final-pin.browser.test.ts:154](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-pin.browser.test.ts:154), [scatter.test.ts:490](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:490) |\n    31\t| C9 · Strip estimate blanks a readable donut | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | The controller measures the reservation and retries without it when needed. The measurement can become stale after a resize. See R11. [controller.ts:1410](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1410), [controller.ts:1462](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1462) | “Measured/estimated strip: no strip is reserved, and the ring is drawn.” Rule 5 and L8 with supplied dimensions. [verify-pass.test.ts:250](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:250) |\n    32\t| C10 · Narrow scatter drops its automatic x endpoint | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | The extent includes missing-y x values and layout can choose a coarser domain. That domain can disagree with the zoom domain. See R8 and R12. [axes.ts:149](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:149), [layout/index.ts:279](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/index.ts:279) | “x 1.1, 8.9, 10.7 with the last y null” and “x −3.3, 7.7 and 1001.5 at … px wide.” F7 and fixture-derived tick expectations. [verify-pass.test.ts:272](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/verify-pass.test.ts:272), [layout.test.ts:755](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts:755) |\n    33\t| C11 · Watcher acquisition gets stuck on reattachment | Major | **Fixed** | Failed acquisition rolls back prior subscriptions and clears `watching` so the next resize retries. [chart.ts:110](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:110) | “A watcher that throws once while it is put back.” DX5/L3 lifecycle expectations and an independently counted listener fixture. [reattach.browser.test.ts:21](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/reattach.browser.test.ts:21) |\n    34\t| C12 · Accounting omits live