r datum under the still pointer…” and “Escape while held.” Rule 3b and the Escape clarification. **None** for stationary rest across same-datum geometry changes. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:241](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:241) |\n    37\t| I7 · Dismissal follows sampled rows | Major | **Partly fixed** | Escape saves the chosen ref and checks beyond the sample, but membership is approximate. Escape from a pin also dismisses an unrelated datum currently under the pointer. See R3–R5. [interaction.ts:1192](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1192), [interaction.ts:1552](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1552) | “Dismiss scatter A, append fifteen coincident B…” Rules 7–8 and fixture. **None** for the reverse sequence or unrelated B. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:290](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:290) |\n    38\t| I8 · Some scatter rows cannot be selected | Major | **Partly fixed** | The reported interleaving works for drawn points. An interleaved point clipped by the y domain has no anchor and stops enumeration. In a nine-member exact group this can still repeat page one. [focus.ts:186](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:186), [interaction.ts:746](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:746) | “Twelve near-coincident points interleaved in x order.” Fixture provides the twelve expected row IDs. **None** for clipped interleaving. [focus-reading.test.ts:89](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/focus-reading.test.ts:89) |\n    39\t| I9 · Pressed or focused tooltip row moves or disappears | Major | **Partly fixed** | Keys survive title reformatting, and open-shadow presses use the composed path. Focus transfer still reads `document.activeElement`, which sees the host in a shadow root. A captured row can also select a different category after remapping. See R1. [tooltip.ts:81](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:81), [tooltip.ts:202](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:202), [interaction.ts:1469](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1469) | “Press its row, append a later coincident B…” uses rule 9 and expects one selection of A. The floating-to-strip test only requires focus somewhere in the chart. **None** for category remapping during a press or shadow-root focus transfer. [final-verify.browser.test.ts:308](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:308), [final-verify.browser.test.ts:331](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:331) |\n    40\t| I10 · Focused text rewrites on an unchanged category | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | A sliding Q3 keeps its text. Distinct categories that format identically can now suppress the required rewrite on eviction. See R10. [focus.ts:215](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:215), [interaction.ts:1932](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1932) | “A narrowed category that slides keeps its reading.” Decision 0004 part 2 requires equality. The browser fixture also checks the original text and new ordinal. [focus-reading.test.ts:111](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/focus-reading.test.ts:111), [final-verify.browser.test.ts:352](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-verify.browser.test.ts:352) |\n    41\t| I11 · Strip reservation removes a readable plot | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | The supplied 112 px plot stays readable with readout mode `none`. Resizing can leave `none` selected after the strip becomes short enough to fit. See R11. [controller.ts:1426](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1426), [controller