{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show 9f9eeef:docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | rg -n '\"'^(#{1,}|.*(lookup|interaction|controller|Store).*)'\"' | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Phase 2 plan: Axylo 1.0 in TypeScript\n9:## 1. Public API\n13:### 1.1 Shape\n38:### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\n63:### 1.3 Fields\n90:### 1.4 Common options\n107:### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\n130:### 1.6 Diagnostics\n149:### 1.7 React adapter (not in 1.0)\n169:## 2. Architecture\n171:### 2.1 Pipeline\n176:            ▼ diagnostics                ├─► lookup: exact values by x, by point, by ordinal\n187:| lookup | Nearest-x by binary search; nearest-point by a grid index (scatter) | Works on the frame within the visible range; cost bounded independently of the drawing. |\n192:### 2.2 Invalidation\n206:### 2.3 Rendering\n218:### 2.4 Document structure\n241:### 2.5 Repository\n257:## 3. Milestones\n261:### M0. Foundations (ceiling: 5 days)\n270:### M1. A vertical slice, and the two open decisions (ceiling: 12 days)\n273:- A minimal tooltip and one keyboard path, enough to exercise lookup and focus end to end.\n281:- Two written decision records, each with its measurements: the renderer, and the plot's interaction pattern. Each says what was observed and what was inferred.\n286:### M2. Faithful data, on the line chart (ceiling: 8 days)\n298:### M3. Reading the chart (ceiling: 10 days)\n311:### M4. Accessibility, complete on the line chart (ceiling: 10 days)\n324:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\n338:### M6. Updates and scale (ceiling: 10 days)\n350:### M7. Distribution and documentation (ceiling: 8 days)\n361:### M8. Release (ceiling: 10 days)\n372:## 4. Test strategy\n388:## 5. Risks\n392:| The interaction pattern that works in one screen reader fails in another. | Three candidates rehearsed on five pairs in M1, before any of the surrounding DOM is built. Plot roles are internal and can change in a minor release. |\n395:| The million-point budget cannot be met with exact lookup and gap-preserving simplification. | The headline claim is already limited to measured workloads (spec, section 1). If P2 fails after tuning, the budget is changed in the spec with the measurements, not hidden. |\n400:## 6. What waits until after 1.0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
