{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_134","type":"agent_message","text":"## 1. The five blockers\n\nRead-only review of `9f9eeef`. All line numbers refer to that commit. The full suite and browser cases were assessed from source and the authors’ pre-fix results. The in-memory Node checks ended with:\n\n```text\n6 of 6 read-only Node probes matched expectations at 9f9eeef\n1 of 1 additional read-only Node probes matched expectations at 9f9eeef\n```\n\n| Item | Verdict and smallest remaining fix | Revert test and basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| **C2** | **Partly fixed.** Showing the same paused revision preserves the baseline. But draw scatter x=101 with `keep: 1`, pause, then repeatedly hide, append late x=0, and show. After 100 cycles I observed **one retained row and 101 revision sources**. The row-count threshold never fires. Also trigger freezing when the span of retained revisions exceeds a bound. [controller.ts:1641](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1641), [controller.ts:1665](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1665), [store-rows.ts:434](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-rows.ts:434) | The 100 increasing-x cycles catch the baseline revert. The paused and resumed rows come from spec I6 and the fixture. `2 × baseline + 8` is implementation policy. The test counts rows only. [round3.test.ts:28](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/round3.test.ts:28) |\n| **I4** | **Partly fixed.** Pin two short series on one strip line in a card that clips horizontally just after the first row. The strip passes even if the second button is cut off, because only row one and any pager are checked. Check every displayed row and the pager against the clipped rectangle inside the row-reduction loop. [tooltip.ts:435](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:435) | The long-title and clipped-sliver tests catch the original regressions. Their geometry comes from Decision 0004 rules 5–6 and the fixtures. The long-title test allows the entire strip to disappear. [final-round3.browser.test.ts:231](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts:231), [final-round3.browser.test.ts:246](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts:246) |\n| **I5** | **Partly fixed.** Open slots and shared scaling are handled. Focus a top-toolbar button styled with a 32 px outline, then hover a datum whose tooltip fits 24 px from the button. The tooltip can cover the outline because placement budgets only 3 px at 1×. Use the control’s computed outline width and offset in its own scale. [mapping.ts:95](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/mapping.ts:95), [interaction.ts:879](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:879) | The slot test catches the clipping-walk revert when a tooltip appears. Its bounds come from Decision 0004 rules 2 and 10. The painted-outline branch has no regression test. [final-round3.browser.test.ts:269](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts:269) |\n| **R1** | **Partly fixed.** A surviving button selects the remapped Q3, and subsequent keyboard activation works. A redraw that moves the same row between presentations can still lose the press. See item 3 below. [tooltip.ts:150](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:150), [tooltip.ts:218](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:218) | The Q3 slide and immediate Enter tests catch the two original reverts. The expected selections follow Decision 0004 rule 9 and the fixtures. [final-round3.browser.test.ts:140](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts:140), [final-round3.browser.test.ts:163](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts:163) |\n| **R2** | **Fixed for the original open-shadow case.** Focus is resolved through the open root before the drag, range, or tooltip branch can consume Escape. [attributes.ts:14](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/attributes.ts:14), [interaction.ts:1567](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1567) | Pin A in the open root, hover B, and press Escape. A closes and B stays open, as required by Decision 0004’s focused-chart clarification. [final-round3.browser.test.ts:181](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-round3.browser.test.ts:181) |\n\n## 2. Defects introduced by this round\n\n1. **AX160 can keep a fixed-height chart redrawing.** Give y an explicit `[0, 10]` domain and a tick formatter that throws at 2. At a height where the disclosure note forces sparser ticks, the note removes tick 2, which removes the note, which brings tick 2 back. The Node host alternated between 121 px and 101 px plots with simulated resize notifications. Keep tick-only AX160 as a diagnostic with effect `none` so the note cannot change the fit. [controller.ts:1552](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1552), [chart.ts:239](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:239)\n2. **A pinned scatter pager can repeat page one.** At DPR 1, pin a point at horizontal offset 0.8 px. Append eight at offset 0 and the latest at 0.4 px, all at the same y with fixed axes. The redraw takes the middle point’s count of ten but makes the pinned point the paging anchor. That anchor has only two members, so `+2 more` returns to page one. Keep the lookup’s anchor, sample, and count together and track the pinned ref separately. [interaction.ts:1947](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1947), [interaction.ts:778](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:778)\n3. **A press can disappear during a resize.** Press Q3’s floating row, shrink the chart into strip mode while holding it, then release over the new Q3 strip button. The redraw deletes the captured entry, so no selection fires. Keep the row’s semantic identity for the life of the pin and resolve it in the current presentation on release. Bind click suppression to that press. [interaction.ts:2097](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:2097), [tooltip.ts:218](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:218)\n4. **An append can undo a narrow scatter zoom.** On the R8 fixture, zoom to `[-1000, 1500]` and append x=1600. The window jumps to `[-500, 2000]` and admits the new point. I observed this in Node. Preserve the drawn bounds for the current zoom across appends and extend them when the data grows. [controller.ts:504](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:504)\n5. **Changing `x.format` leaves stale keyboard text.** Focus Q1 in the default all-series mode and change its formatter to say “Quarter Q1.” The tooltip updates, but `aria-valuetext` keeps “Q1” because the comparison key only keeps raw x. Include both raw x and formatted x in the key. [focus.ts:176](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:176), [interaction.ts:948](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:948)\n6. **Scatter zoom rebuilds indexes for off-screen data.** Zoom a multi-month scatter to one day, with more than 32 measurements sharing a date. Each zoom or pan rebuilds the full-series row map and allocates a reverse grid index for all points. Reuse row indexes across views of the same frame and size the grid index to visible ranges. [scatter.ts:40](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter.ts:40), [scatter-grid.ts:74](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:74), [controller.ts:1568](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1568)\n\n## 3. Earlier findings\n\nStatuses refer to the earlier repro